<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camilo Torres Tenorio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1766–<a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Camilo Torres Tenorio was a lawyer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popayan">Popayán</a> and a leading figure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>'s independence movement. His Memorial de Agravios of 1809 protested against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s unequal treatment of the American colonies. He led the federalist congress of the United Provinces of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> and served as its president, and was executed by the Spanish reconquest forces in 1816.</p></div>
